Got it!

I started this game quite sometime back now, maybe it has been more than a 
month. Did not keep notes so I do not remember much of the early game and 
bits and pieces in between.

The start was nothing extraordinary, no spellbook of magic missile or ring 
of slow digestion or conflict in starting inventory, got a magic marker 
though. My wizard had intelligence of 18 so spellcasting was hungerless from 
the beginning. First part of the game went OK I guess cause there is no 
specific incident I remember.

Oracle level was really helpful as a lot of spellbooks were obtained from 
the statues there, something like 3-4 spellbooks, one of which was a 
spellbook of create monster and another was a spellbook of magic missile. 
Completed Sokoban hoping to get a bag of holding to put the spellbooks into 
but got amulet of reflection.

Dived into the mines and went to Minetown (Grotto Town), no magic lamp in 
the shops but temple was co-aligned. So promptly sacrificed and got 
Magicbane. Went to Mines' End and got the luckstone. Came back to Minetown 
and maximized luck. Also got a magic lamp somewhere below Minetown, blessed 
it and used that as a source of light for the rest of the game.

Then the wizard's journey continued onwards into the main branch.

Found the magic portal to quest on Dlvl:14 and immediately completed it. The 
Dark One gave some trouble, my plan of catching him asleep and frying him 
with multiple, reflected magic missiles, forcing him to abandon the Eye of 
Aethiopica, failed. So went toe-to-toe with him and managed to kill him. I 
now believe what they say, the Dark One has never killed anyone, ever ;)

Continuing the journey, found portal to Fort Ludios on Dlvl:23. Came right 
back as my wizard was in no shape to take on the inhabitants of the fort at 
that time.

Now somewhere I got a ring of slow digestion so decided to do some 
sacrificing to appease Thoth. Sacfest in Minetown continued with the ring of 
slow digestion on. Got several artifact weapons like Giantslayer, Vorpal 
Blade, Cleaver, Wearbane, Trollsbane, Sunsword and finally Frost Brand. 
Started praying for spellbooks after maximizing luck and got crowned. 
Received a spellbook of finger of death as the crowning gift. Recieved 
several useful spellbooks from Thoth like charm monster, extra healing, 
remove curse, cure sickness, jump, cancellation, magic mapping etc.

And then while the sacfest continued, a brown pudding was generated. I had 
never tried pudding farming before so I thought, let's try it. Almost filled 
up the entire level with brown puddings and killed and sacrificed some, you 
know, tested the waters a bit. Got several scrolls of enchant armor and 
enchant weapon and many random useless potions to create holy water.
Also learned the pass-tune to the Castle drawbridge.

Equipped to tackle the Castle level, my wizard completed Medusa (Titan 
version). Titan was given the finger and scrolls of earth from Sokoban and 
elsewhere helped reach Medusa (my wizard had no levitation at that point but 
did knew the spell of jumping but I did not use that). With Medusa dead the 
wizard entered the Castle.
An Arch-Lich promptly warped next to me and started generating nasties, I 
just got a lot of new pets and finished the Arch-Lich with their help. 
Cleared Castle, got the wand and wished for scrolls of charging, speed 
boots, helm of brilliance, gauntlets of dexterity and SDSM.

Then took the wizard back to Ludios to say hello to the soldiers and their 
leader Croesus. Using the gold brought protection from the co-aligned priest 
in Minetown. More sacrificing was conducted and got spellbooks of identify 
and polymorph amongst others.

Then back through the Dungeons of Doom finally reached the Valley. Went 
straight to Gehennom and killed Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Juiblex and Orcus would 
Vlad's tower and got the Candelabrum. Found portal to Wizard's Tower and 
identified vibrating square. Gehennom went very fast due the spellbook magic 
mapping.

I had established stash in Sokoban and since I had never tried polypiling 
before decided to try that too. My wizard was yet to find a ring of free 
action, a ring of conflict, scroll of genocide and he needed another 
spellbook of magic missile pretty urgently so I hoped to get some magic 
markers as well. I hoped to get a shirt/T-shirt as well. Did some polypiling 
and got a T-shirt, scrolls of genocide, ring of free action but no more 
magic markers of a ring of conflict was were found, by polypiling or 
otherwise. Made a typo while polypiling and polymorphed self into a silver 
dragon losing a blessed fireproof +5 T-shirt and blessed fireproof +4 cloak 
of magic resistance. Had found another magic lamp somewhere to used that to 
wish for another cloak of magic resistance. Polypiled some more and got a 
Hawaiian shirt and couple of spellbooks of magic missile.

Also performed alchemy for the first time and after quaffing 10 or so I kept 
17 more blessed diluted potions of full healing. They remained that way till 
the end, never had to use them.

Then went back to the Minetown temple to get some intrinsic protection but I 
am not sure what happened and at some point I realized that my wizard had 
lost all of his divine protection. I do not know what happened there.
So had his pets kill the priest and reclaimed all of the gold. Also got a 
robe which was fixed and enchanted up and replaced the cloak of magic 
resistance. Purchased divine protection anew from the priestess at the 
Valley. Enchanted up a small shield as well and achieved an comfortable AC 
of -45.

At some point blessed genocided L,h and R. Kept two uncursed scrolls of 
genocide to curse and reverse genocide purple worms on Astral plane.

Then killed the Wizard of Yendor and performed invocation and retrieved the 
amulet. Quaffed a cursed potion of gain level and started the ascension run. 
Rodney did not make his first appearance after death until I was almost out 
of Gehennom. Mysterious force was not bad at all, pulled back my wizard only 
two or three times and that too only one level down.

Went to stash in Sokoban on the way up and collected all required things and 
entered the plane of earth. Gave Rodney the finger again and completed it 
easily.
Plane of air was a little challenging without conflict but fortunately only 
a couple of air elementals caused significant damage.
Plane of fire was pretty uneventful.
Upon entering the plane of water I blessed one scroll of genocide and 
genocided all ; to be safe. Found the portal to Astral and on my wizard 
went.

Upon entering Astral I encountered a kuge with AC -29 and 100+ health and 
reflection. Killing him with Frost Brand was not a very appealing prospect 
so cast drain life upon him till he croaked.
Death was assigned to the central altar, Famine to the left one and 
Pestilence to the right one. I had a helm of opposite alignment and was 
prepared to use it.

I decided to go left towards Famine. There was no need to fight Famine as he 
was diametrically opposite to the entrance to altar room when I got there 
and did not get too close. I never had to use the helm of opposite 
alignment, for that was the high altar of Thoth.

